"Transcript_Log": "Agent: Hello, Duroflex Indiranagar.\nCustomer: Yeah, hi. I'm looking for a mattress, can you help me?\nAgent: Yes, sure sir.\nCustomer: What is your name?\nAgent: [Inaudible/Mumbled]... Vinod sir.\nCustomer: Vinod, okay. Vinod, we are looking for a mattress which is 75 by 60.\nAgent: 75 by 60. Okay.\nCustomer: Slightly bigger than Queen, almost like a Queen. So I want to know, there are a lot of different materials. We want little more... not very hot, but little firm. So ideally we prefer something like Coir and Latex combination.\nAgent: Sir, Coir and Latex combination comes in the Natural Living range. That is the 'Tatva' model. But if you want firm, we can go with the Duropedic range.\nCustomer: What is the material in Duropedic?\nAgent: Material is having memory foam and also bonded foam with Coir.\nCustomer: No, we want Coir and Foam? Coir and Latex will be expensive is it?\nAgent: Latex will come in Natural Living. There you will get that one. It has Latex and you will get a spring in that.\nCustomer: We don't need spring.\nAgent: Okay fine sir. If you can go with this one... in Latex also we have bonded foam based. There you will not get Coir, but bonded foam.\nCustomer: But if you go with Duropedic kind of thing?\nAgent: Where you get back support, you will get a Coir base on that.\nCustomer: So Coir and Foam is one option. What is the other option?\nAgent: Coir and Latex is not there. Latex and Bonded foam is there.\nCustomer: I can see Natural Latex and Coir as an option... 'Tatva'.\nAgent: Tatva... okay one second. Yeah, in Tatva you will get Coir and Foam combination.\nCustomer: But it is very expensive?\nAgent: Yeah, a bit expensive sir. It comes in premium category.\nCustomer: What is the normal product? Not so expensive.\nAgent: You can go with Duropedic. Where you have Balance... Strength Plus.\nCustomer: What material is that?\nAgent: That is a combination of Memory Foam and Coir. Bonded foam is also there.\nCustomer: Memory foam and Coir... okay. Will Latex be better and more comfortable?\nAgent: Latex will give little bit coolness and softness on top. Memory foam also gives softness but helps for back support.\nCustomer: Okay. And what is the warranty?\nAgent: Strength Plus we have 7 to 10 years warranty based on category.\nCustomer: Strength Plus is how many inches?\nAgent: Strength Plus you will get around 8 inches.\nCustomer: That is also 36,000. Is there any discount?\nAgent: For 75 by 60... cost is around 37,720.\nCustomer: Any discount? I am seeing some HDFC card offer.\nAgent: Apart from that you will get card offer. Card offer is around 35,000... wait.\nCustomer: I am seeing something like 60% off. What is that?\nAgent: HDFC showing 60% off? Let me check sir. Usually sale is going 15 to 20%.\nCustomer: Today is 16th... already 17th. Let me check and give a call back?\nAgent: Yeah sure sir. Can you give me your number?\nCustomer: 98450...\nAgent: [Repeats number]. You are Vinod right?\nCustomer: Yeah right. So is there a pure latex option?\nAgent: Yes sir, 100% latex. Prana.\nCustomer: Prana is very expensive. Any other one?\nAgent: What range you are looking?\nCustomer: Nothing like that... not so expensive. I am seeing Latex mattress in 'LiveIn' at 15,000 also. What is that?\nAgent: LiveIn is a basic version. Latex and HR foam. No Coir.\nCustomer: Will it be too soft?\nAgent: Medium soft.\nCustomer: What is Cube Cell?\nAgent: Cube cell acts like a spring. Instead of spring we use foam which gives firmness.\nCustomer: Okay. Can you check on this HDFC offer and call me back?\nAgent: Sure sir. Is there anything like Latex + Coir you can suggest?\nCustomer: Yeah.\nAgent: Okay sir I will check and call you back."
}

